&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re TechnologyAdvice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee, TechnologyAdvice helps millions of B2B technology buyers make smarter decisions by providing trusted research, practical guidance, and connections to the world&#39;s leading technology brands. Our work spans 30+ media brands and 50+ newsletters, supported by a global team across the United States, United Kingdom, Singapore, Australia, and the Philippines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a remote-first company that values curiosity, collaboration, and growth. We invest in our people, embrace AI and new technologies to improve how we work, and create opportunities for team members to build meaningful careers. Many of our leaders have grown from within, including our CEO, who started here as an intern.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel connected. Through company all-hands, team events, Slack communities, learning sessions, and in-person gatherings, we create intentional opportunities for our global team to collaborate, build relationships, and celebrate successes together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All positions are open to remote work unless otherwise specified in the requirements below.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Channel Insider, part of TechnologyAdvice, is looking for an experienced Account Director to become the first dedicated EMEA channel sales specialist within our growing EMEA business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to step into a senior, highly visible, first feet on the ground role with the mandate to help shape, launch, and scale Channel Insider’s EMEA commercial presence. You will join TechnologyAdvice at an exciting stage of growth, with the backing of an established global business, a strong brand portfolio, proven demand generation capabilities, and a leadership team committed to building something meaningful in the EMEA channel market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, quota-carrying role with ownership of the full sales cycle. You will identify and develop high-value client relationships, engage senior marketing and channel decision-makers, uncover commercial challenges, and position tailored solutions across digital brand, content, events, audience engagement, and demand generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will be someone who knows the channel ecosystem, understands how vendors and partners go to market, and can bring credibility, confidence, and commercial energy into senior client conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While you will be accountable for your own revenue number, you will not be building in isolation. You will have the support of TechnologyAdvice’s senior leadership, client success, delivery, marketing, StudioA, product, sales enablement, SDRs, and the wider global business. This is a role for someone who wants own

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Contentstack?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contentstack is redefining how modern digital experiences are built and managed. As the pioneer of the Agentic Experience Platform (AXP), Contentstack brings together structured content and brand governance (Content Cloud), real-time customer data, omnichannel personalization (Data Cloud) and autonomous AI orchestration (Agent OS) into one unified system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While many organizations adopted headless CMS or standalone AI tools expecting transformation, they often found themselves managing disconnected systems and manual workflows. Contentstack helps enterprises move beyond that complexity by connecting content, data and AI in a way that makes digital experiences faster to launch, easier to manage and more adaptive in real time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leading brands including Steve Madden, LG Electronics, Subaru of America, Dolce &amp;amp; Gabbana, ASICS, Decathlon, and Caesars Entertainment rely on Contentstack to reduce operational friction and deliver personalized, scalable digital experiences with confidence. The company is known for its customer-first culture and commitment to the communities it serves through the Contentstack Cares program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://www.contentstack.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://www.contentstack.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.contentstack.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Contentstack we are more than colleagues, we are a tribe. Our vision is to pursue equity among our communities, employees, partners, and customers. We are global-diverse yet close; distributed yet connected. We are dreamers and dreammakers who challenge the status quo. We do the right thing, even when no one is watching. We are curious trendspotters and brave trendsetters. Our mission is to make Contentstack indispensable for organizations to tell their stories and to connect with the people they care about through inspiring, modern experiences. We care deeply about our customers and the communities we serve. #OneTeamOneDream. Chalo, let’s go!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;What Are We Looking For?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
